# Production build config for the trade-agent frontend. Vite loads this ONLY for `vite build`
# (production mode) - never for `vite dev` or the test runner, so local dev keeps the same-origin
# "/api" default.
#
# Split-origin production wiring: the browser is served from https://trade-agent.samir.codes
# (Firebase Hosting behind Cloudflare's CDN) and calls the API cross-origin at the api. subdomain.
# That subdomain is Cloudflare grey-cloud (DNS-only) -> Cloud Run, so the SSE reasoning stream is
# not buffered by a CDN and arrives frame-by-frame. The backend CORS-allowlists this frontend
# origin (backend PROD_FRONTEND_ORIGINS); see docs/DESIGN_DECISIONS.md.
#
# This value is public DNS, NOT a secret, so it is committed for a reproducible production build.
# The Firebase public identifiers are deliberately NOT duplicated here - they come from the
# machine-local .env.local, which Vite also loads during `vite build`.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.trade-agent.samir.codes/api
